				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />
<span style="color: blue"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: normal"><span style="font-weight: bold">Want to Join MoKB?</span></span></span>
<br />
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
Greetings from the Minions of Kaer Baar and the Recruiting Committee. The following is subject to change. The recruiting requirements last changed on: <span style="color: red">October 28, 2004</span>. Additional requirements that occur only affect new, incoming applicants. All questions should be directed to the <a href="http://www.mokb.org/phpbb/privmsg.php?mode=post&amp;u=29" target="_blank" class="postlink">Recruiting Committee</a> (RC) or an Officer via Private Message (PM).
<br />
<ul><li>Please read "About MoKB". Here is the link: <a href="http://www.mokb.org/phpbb/viewtopic.php?p=63411#63411" target="_blank" class="postlink">About MoKB</a>
<br />

<br />
<li>Applications posted in the Public Forum may be moved for review. Please dont panic and wonder where your thread went.
<br />

<br />
<li>Applicants are welcome to join MoKB on raids. Please contact the RC or an Officer if you wish to attend.
<br />
</ul>Every member of MoKB goes through a series of stages before becoming a Full Member. The first stage is the Application process. The second stage is the Recruit process. Every Recruit carries the MoKB tag, and only the recruit's main character is guilded. All Recruits are to refrain from using full anonymous. The final stage is the vote for Full Membership.
<br />

<br />
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />
<span style="color: blue"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: normal"><span style="font-weight: bold">Applications</span></span></span>
<br />
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />
<ul><li>During the recruit process, both the recruit and guild invest a lot in the process. We want to be sure that each applicant is knowledgable and committed to recruiting. If an applicant has any questions, we want to answer them before a committment is made. For this reason, applications will not be accepted from people still wearing a guild tag or have applied to multiple guilds. <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">When registering on these boards, please use a login name that matches your main character's name.</span></span> Otherwise, things get confusing.
<br />

<br />
<li> MoKB looks at the whole package when recruiting, so please do not hesitate to apply. Each Applicant must have a full member as a sponsor. If you do not have a sponsor, contact an RC member and a sponsor may be assigned. The Recruiting Committee realizes that on occasion people come to us as partners or groups. Partners may be given the option of "joint application" under one Sponsor. 
<br />

<br />
<li>The Applicant must pass an initial examination and interview with the Recruiting Committee. Everything from reputation and history to gear and skills may be examined. 
<br />
</ul><span style="color: blue">Flag(s) required for Application</span> : PoJ Trial, Hedge Walk
<br />
(<span style="font-style: italic">Class</span> - Minimum Level Required - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> or  <span style="color: red"><span style="font-weight: bold">CLOSED</span></span> - Required AA's for Application)
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Bard</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Beastlord</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Bezerker</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Cleric</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Druid</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Enchanter</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Magician</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Monk</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Necromancer</span> - 63  - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Paladin</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Ranger</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span>- Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Rogue</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Shadowknight</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Shaman</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Warrior</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span>- Run 3, AoE Taunt
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Wizard</span> - 63 - <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> - Run 3
<br />

<br />
Classes that are listed as <span style="color: green"><span style="font-weight: bold">OPEN</span></span> are accepted under normal conditions. Classes that are listed as <span style="color: red"><span style="font-weight: bold">CLOSED</span></span> will be examined on a case-by-case basis. There is a limit of <span style="font-weight: bold">50 (fifty)</span> Recruits allowed into the system at one time. When the guild is at limit, applications will be added, in order of acceptance, to a list kept by the Recruiting Committee. When a spot becomes available, a PM will be sent to the Sponsor.  Sponsors will be given <span style="font-weight: bold">3 (three)</span> days to respond. After three days, the Applicant will be bumped down one spot on the list. The following requirements must be met for all Sponsors:<ul><li>The prospective Sponsor must be a Full Member for at least 3 weeks and an active player. Active Sponsors lead to active Recruits.
<br />

<br />
<li>A Sponsor may only sponsor a maximum of <span style="font-weight: bold">2</span> Recruits.
<br />

<br />
<li>Joint or Grouped Recruits will be treated as <span style="font-weight: bold">1</span> Recruit. Joint Recruits will be voted on at the same time for Full Membership once the requirements are met by all of the Recruits involved.
<br />
</ul><img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />
<span style="color: blue"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: normal"><span style="font-weight: bold">Full Membership Vote</span></span></span>
<br />
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1578.gif" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
A Recuit must go through a process of Full Membership Vote (a vote done by all full members) before becoming a Full Member. The following are the minimum requirements that a Recruit must meet before being considered for Full Membership Vote:<ul><li>The Recruit must be guild flagged for a minimum of <span style="font-weight: bold">2 (two)</span> weeks. Attendance on raids, conduct during raids, board participation, playing skill, etc are discussed by full members as part of the membership vote.
<br />

<br />
<li>The Recruit must have the AA's, level, and flag(s) required for Full Member Vote in addition to those required for Application. Recruits must also have created and updated their flags in the MoKB database.
<br />

<br />
<li>When a Recruit has met all of the requirements for Full Membership Vote, the Recruit must PM a request for a Full Membership Vote to the <a href="http://www.mokb.org/phpbb/privmsg.php?mode=post&amp;u=29" target="_blank" class="postlink">Recruiting Committee</a> (and his/her Sponsor) to begin the process.
<br />
</ul><span style="color: blue">Flag(s) required for Full Membership Vote</span> : BoT (PoS Item Collection)
<br />
(<span style="font-style: italic">Class</span> - Minimum Level Required - Required AA's for Full Membership Vote)
<br />

<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Bard</span> - 65 - Fading Memories
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Beastlord</span> - 65 - Pet Discipline 
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Bezerker</span> - 65 - n/a
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Cleric</span> - 65 - MGB
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Druid</span> - 65 - Spirit of the Wood
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Enchanter</span> - 65 - MGB
<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Magician</span> - 65 - Pet Discipline 
